   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state finance law and the education law, in relation to\nthe oversight of certain contracts by the comptroller",
    "basePrintNo": "S2219",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2219-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §112, St Fin L; amd §§355, 373, 6218 & 6275, Ed L (as proposed in S.6809-A & A.7925-A)",
    "lawSection": "State Finance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2219\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state finance law and the education law, in relation\nto the oversight of certain contracts by the comptroller\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to chapter 839 of 2022 by making changes to\nthe contract thresholds that would require comptroller oversight, and to\nshorten the amount of time the comptroller has to review certain\ncontracts by SUNY, CUNY, and their respective construction funds.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of § 112 of the State\nFinance Law to amend the Comptroller's authority to review Office of\nGeneral Services (OGS) centralized contracts to increase the threshold\nfrom $85,000 to $125,000, and a threshold of $200,000 for purchase\norders and other procurement transactions issued under such centralized\ncontract. The time the Comptroller has to review contracts made by the\nState University of New York (SUNY), the SUNY Construction Fund, the\nCity University of New York (CUNY) and the CUNY Construction fund is\nmade 75 days, compared to 90 days for other agencies, with the possibil-\nity of an extension of 15 days or a reasonable time agreed upon between\nthe Comptroller and the agency.\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision 5 of § 355 of the Education Law to increase\nthe threshold for Comptroller approval of SUNY contracts from $50,000 to\n$75,000.\n\nSection 3 amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 16 of § 355 of the Educa-\ntion Law to increase the threshold for Comptroller's oversight for\ncontracts where SUNY is functioning as a health care provider from\n$75,000 to $150,000.\n\nSection 4 amends subdivision 12 of § 373 of the Education Law to set a\nthreshold for Comptroller's oversight for SUNY Construction Fund\ncontracts of $75,000.\n\nSection 5 amends subdivision (a) of § 6218 of the Education Law to set\nthe threshold for Comptroller's oversight for certain CUNY contracts,\nincluding construction contracts, at $75,000.\n\nSection 6 amends subdivision 9 of § 6275 of the Education Law to set a\nthreshold for Comptroller's oversight for CUNY Construction Fund\ncontracts of $75,000.\n\nSection 7 sets the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 839 of the Laws of 2022. S.6809-A passed\nthe Senate in May 2022, and A.7925-A passed the Assembly in June 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022, amending the state finance law and the\neducation law relating to restoring oversight of certain contracts by\nthe comptroller, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6809-A and\nA. 7925-A, takes effect.\n",
